BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[C3] LECTURE: Introduction to Homeostasis 1
DTSTART:20260831T150000Z
DTEND:20260831T155000Z
DTSTAMP:20260903T143736Z
UID:f5278e21-4432-400f-b7c1-f3660445fb84_E198663@calendar.med.ualberta.ca
DESCRIPTION:\nCourse: MED 511\n\nInstructors:\n	Shereen Hamza (shamza)\n\n
 My Group:\n	Name: EDM\n	Location: KHRA 2-190\n\nObjectives:\n	Describe the
  significance of homeostasis in physiology and medicine.\n	Describe the ma
 jor organs\, organ systems and compartments of the human body.\n	Describe 
 the concept of homeostasis as the central organizing principle of physiolo
 gy using examples of key homeostatic processes\, including body fluid dist
 ribution\, blood glucose regulation\, and pH balance\, among others.\n	Out
 line homeostatic control theory including negative feedback control\, rese
 tting of set points\, and feedforward regulation.\n	Describe the significa
 nce of maintaining the stability of the internal environment of the body i
 n the face of changes in the external environment.\n\nView this event onli
 ne: https://calendar.med.ualberta.ca/events/198663
LOCATION:
URL:https://calendar.med.ualberta.ca/events/198663
END:VEVENT
