BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[C3] LECTURE: Weekly Review
DTSTART:20261030T210000Z
DTEND:20261030T215000Z
DTSTAMP:20260903T143736Z
UID:f5278e21-4432-400f-b7c1-f3660445fb84_E198690@calendar.med.ualberta.ca
DESCRIPTION:Welcome to our rapid-fire review session\, designed to efficie
 ntly complement the foundational case studies by enabling the application 
 of knowledge of bacterial classification\, resistance mechanisms\, and the
 rapeutic modes to clinical scenarios. Our primary focus will be on the thr
 ee major bacterial classifications—Gram-positives\, Gram-negatives \, an
 d Atypicals . During the rapid-fire Q&A\, we will apply these structural a
 nd resistance principles to practice selecting appropriate therapeutic mod
 es (Empiric vs. Definitive) and reinforce the core principles of Antimicro
 bial Stewardship (AMS)\, focusing on optimizing patient outcomes by ensuri
 ng we prescribe antibiotics only when necessary\, using the narrowest spec
 trum agent for the shortest effective duration to combat rising antimicrob
 ial resistance.\nCourse: MED 511\n\nInstructors:\n	Roshan Abraham (jrabrah
 a)\n	Shereen Hamza (shamza)\n	William Stokes (wstokes)\n\nMy Group:\n	Name
 : EDM\n	Location: 2-190 KHRA\n\nView this event online: https://calendar.m
 ed.ualberta.ca/events/198690
LOCATION:
URL:https://calendar.med.ualberta.ca/events/198690
END:VEVENT
