DESCRIPTION:\nCourse: MED 511\n\nInstructors:\n	Shereen Hamza (shamza)\n\n
 My Group:\n	Name: EDM\n	Location: KHRA 2-190\n\nObjectives:\n	Describe the
  organization of the cardiovascular system including the heart and vascula
 ture as key effectors.\n	Apply principles of fluid dynamics including bloo
 d flow\, pressure gradients and vascular resistance.\n	Describe the anatom
 ical structures of the heart including: gross anatomy\, chambers\, valves\
 , path of blood flow.\n	Explain the mechanics of cardiac function includin
 g the steps of the cardiac cycle.\n	Describe the physiology of cardiac mus
 cle including innervation and blood supply.\n	Explain the determinants of 
 cardiac output and its control.\n	Describe the organization of the vascula
 ture\, properties of arteries\, arterioles\, capillaries\, venules and vei
 ns.\n	Explain the purpose and function of the lymphatic system including i
 ts contribution in supporting cardiovascular function.\n	Apply principles 
 of the integrative function of the cardiovascular system including short a
 nd long-term control of blood pressure and volume.\n\nView this event onli
 ne: https://calendar.med.ualberta.ca/events/198694
LOCATION:
URL:https://calendar.med.ualberta.ca/events/198694
