SUMMARY:[C3] LECTURE: DNA Damage and Repair 1
DTSTART:20260928T160000Z
DTEND:20260928T165000Z
DTSTAMP:20260903T143736Z
UID:f5278e21-4432-400f-b7c1-f3660445fb84_E198735@calendar.med.ualberta.ca
DESCRIPTION:\nCourse: MED 511\n\nInstructors:\n	Adrienne Wright (awright)\
 n\nMy Group:\n	Name: EDM\n	Location: 1080 Katz\n\nObjectives:\n	Describe w
 hy it is important that DNA double-stranded structure is stabilized by non
 -covalent interactions.\n	Explain how the structure of DNA allows for spec
 ific binding of DNA binding proteins.\n	Describe the function of the codin
 g strand and the template strand in transcription.\n	Define the terms prom
 oter and transcription factor.\n	Describe the function of tRNA in translat
 ion.\n	Define the terms codon and ‘reading frame’ and use an example t
 o explain how one mRNA sequence can have 3 distinct reading frames.\n	Expl
 ain how a tRNA carries the correct amino acid.\n	Discuss the terms mis-sen
 se\, non-sense and frame-shift with respect to clinical scenarios.\n	Descr
 ibe the steps involved in the retroviral infection of a mammalian cell.\n	
 Define the terms constitutive genes\, tissue-specific genes and inducible 
 genes.\n	Describe the role of promoters\, transcription factors and enhanc
 ers in the regulation of gene expression.\n	Explain the principles behind 
 “positive” regulation of transcription.\n	Describe why chromatin-remod
 eling is required in regulation of gene expression.\n	Explain how acetylat
 ion of histones leads to the decondensation of chromatin.\n	Explain the me
 chanism of action of steroid hormones.\n	Discuss the major causes and cons
 equences of mutations in DNA in a clinical context.\n	Explain what DNA pol
 ymerases ‘do’ when they “proof-read”.\n	Describe the role of antio
 xidants in minimizing DNA damage.\n	Define the term proto-oncogene.\n	Desc
 ribe how mutations can convert a proto-oncogene to an oncogene.\n	Describe
  DNA repair mechanisms in eukaryotes and the damage they repair.\n	Describ
 e how a virus can cause cancer.\n\nView this event online: https://calenda
 r.med.ualberta.ca/events/198735
LOCATION:
URL:https://calendar.med.ualberta.ca/events/198735
END:VEVENT
