 y Group:\n	Name: EDM\n	Location: 2-190 KHRA\n\nObjectives:\n	Describe diff
 erent types of transfusions and blood products available (blood components
  vs. plasma fractionation products).\n	Describe the blood system in Canada
  with respect to the role of the blood operator and the hospital transfusi
 on service.\n	Describe the tests that are performed as part of pre-transfu
 sion testing (type\, screen and crossmatch).\n	Identify the major blood gr
 oups based on the ABO and Rh D system and how they are tested in the blood
  bank.\n	Describe how the antibody screen is used to detect non-ABO red ce
 ll antibodies.\n	Describe what a crossmatch is and the two different ways 
 this may be performed.\n	Recognize how transfusion reactions may present a
 t the bedside.\n	Describe the general approach and immediate actions to ta
 ke in a transfusion reaction.\n	Develop a differential diagnosis for fever
  and dyspnea associated with transfusion.\n	Describe the pathophysiology o
 f the following transfusion reactions: Acute hemolytic transfusion reactio
 n\; Delayed hemolytic transfusion reaction\; Febrile non-hemolytic transfu
 sion reaction\; Bacterial contamination (BACON).\n	Describe the concept of
  transfusion safety from vein-to-vein.\n\nView this event online: https://
 calendar.med.ualberta.ca/events/198753
LOCATION:
URL:https://calendar.med.ualberta.ca/events/198753
