BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[C3] LECTURE: Case Study:  Intro to Bacteria
DTSTART:20261030T190000Z
DTEND:20261030T205000Z
DTSTAMP:20260903T143736Z
UID:f5278e21-4432-400f-b7c1-f3660445fb84_E198786@calendar.med.ualberta.ca
DESCRIPTION:The Week 10 Case Study session is a practical\, yet deeper div
 e into Week 10 material\, utilizing clinical scenarios and polling to gene
 rate discussion The central purpose is for students to actively apply know
 ledge of bacterial classification\, resistance mechanisms\, and therapeuti
 c modes to patient presentations. This approach reinforces the core princi
 ples of Antimicrobial Stewardship (AMS) by requiring the synthesis of basi
 c science with clinical management decisions.\nCourse: MED 511\n\nInstruct
 ors:\n	Roshan Abraham (jrabraha)\n	William Stokes (wstokes)\n\nMy Group:\n
 	Name: EDM\n	Location: 2-190 KHRA\n\nObjectives:\n	Interpret a gram stain 
 to determine the possible microbial etiology and most appropriate empiric 
 treatment for common infections.\n	Describe the pathogenesis of common inf
 ections\, including pneumonia\, cellulitis\, and appendicitis.\n	Describe 
 4 common causes of antibiotic failure when treating infections.\n\nView th
 is event online: https://calendar.med.ualberta.ca/events/198786
LOCATION:
URL:https://calendar.med.ualberta.ca/events/198786
END:VEVENT
