 es from human cells.\n	Define dimorphic fungi.\n	List 4 classes of fungal 
 diseases (superficial\, subcutaneous\, opportunistic\, endemic).\n	List ri
 sk factors for invasive fungal infections (immunosuppression\, promotion o
 f fungal colonization with antibiotic use\, providing access to blood and 
 organs with catheters).\n\nView this event online: https://calendar.med.ua
 lberta.ca/events/198801
LOCATION:
URL:https://calendar.med.ualberta.ca/events/198801
END:VEVENT
