BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[C3] LECTURE: Sickle Cell Anemia
DTSTART:20261021T170000Z
DTEND:20261021T175000Z
DTSTAMP:20260903T143736Z
UID:f5278e21-4432-400f-b7c1-f3660445fb84_E198892@calendar.med.ualberta.ca
DESCRIPTION:\nCourse: MED 511\n\nInstructors:\n	Linda Sun (lsun3)\n\nMy Gr
 oup:\n	Name: EDM\n	Location: 1080 Katz\n\nObjectives:\n	Discuss the geneti
 cs\, pathophysiology\, and natural history of sickle cell disease.\n	Contr
 ast sickle cell disease and sickle cell trait.\n	Describe the global impac
 t of sickle cell disease\, and recognize the increasing prevalence of pati
 ents living with sickle cell disease in Canada.\n	Describe common and life
 -threatening complications from sickle cell disease (e.g. vaso-occlusive c
 risis\, acute chest syndrome\, stroke).\n	Outline management strategies fo
 r sickle cell disease to manage acute complications and to reduce risk of 
 future harm\, and recognize global disparities in care.\n	Forecast the tre
 atment horizon for sickle cell disease including options for cure (e.g. al
 logeneic stem cell transplant\, gene therapy).\n\nView this event online: 
 https://calendar.med.ualberta.ca/events/198892
LOCATION:
URL:https://calendar.med.ualberta.ca/events/198892
END:VEVENT
